          body: "A 42-year-old felt a twinge in the left side of her neck while reversing her car four days ago. The ache has spread to behind her left eye. Yesterday her right hand went weak for 20 minutes and she could not find her words. She is young, fit, and has no vascular risk factors. Why would a minor neck movement lead to a stroke warning?",
